(a) With respect to existing licenses, mandatory penalties for "due cause" findings by the mayor shall be as follows:
(1) First violation—Minimum of five days to a maximum 180 days suspension of license and $1,000.00 fine; or license revocation;
(2) Second violation—Minimum of 30 days to a maximum of one year suspension of license and $1,000.00 fine; or license revocation;
(3) Third violation—License revocation.
(b) With respect to existing licenses, mandatory penalties for "due cause" findings by the mayor with respect to licensees holding a license to sell alcoholic beverages for on-premises consumption shall be as follows:
(1) First violation—Minimum of five days to a maximum of 180 days suspension of license and $2,500.00 fine; or license revocation;
(2) Second violation—Minimum of 30 days to a maximum of one year suspension of license and $2,500.00 fine; or license revocation;
(3) Third violation—License revocation.
(c) (1) For the purposes of this section, the number of violations shall be cumulative during the time that the alcohol license is held by the licensee and shall not reset at the beginning of each license year.
(2) For the purposes of this section, any suspension or revocation issued in accordance herewith shall be imposed 14 days following the final decision of the mayor.
